# Build output.
build/
sdkconfig
sdkconfig.old

# Resolved by the ESP-IDF component manager during project(). Committing the
# lock file would pin dependencies, which is sometimes wanted - but this tree
# already pins the versions that matter in main/idf_component.yml, and the
# manager rewrites managed_components/ whenever it re-resolves, so anything
# committed there is overwritten without warning.
managed_components/
dependencies.lock

# Cloned by CMakeLists.txt before project(). A committed copy would shadow the
# clone with a stale one.
components/sunset/sunset/

# Derived by CMakeLists.txt from $IDF_PATH at configure time, and re-derived
# whenever the IDF version changes - see the MAP_FATFS_EXFAT block.
#
# Deliberately ignored, unlike the advice in the example this was ported from.
# That advice assumes a script somebody has to remember to run, where an
# uncommitted copy means a fresh clone silently builds FAT-only. Here the copy
# is made automatically, so committing it would only pin a fork of one of IDF's
# components to whichever IDF was installed the day it was made. The patch that
# produces it lives in tools/patch_ffconf.py, which is committed.
components/fatfs/
